<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archdiocese of Trento</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Diocese of Trent</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Archdiocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trento</a> is a Catholic see in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, traced back to the 4th century, when Saint Vigilius was among its early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>. From 1027 its bishops were also princes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, ruling a territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adige">Adige</a> valley until secularisation in 1803. The city hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a> from 1545 to 1563. The diocese was raised to an archdiocese in 1929.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/archdiocese-of-trento.jpg" alt="Archdiocese of Trento" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matteo Ianeselli · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trento-Piazza_del_Duomo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
